  "notes": "{編|あ}む means to create fabric or patterns by interlocking loops or strands — knitting, crocheting, braiding, or weaving by hand.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: [item]を{編|あ}む\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{編|あ}んでいる can mean \"is knitting\" (action in progress) or \"has been knitted\" (result), depending on context.\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- {編|あ}み{物|もの}: knitting, knitted item\n- {手編|てあ}み: hand-knitted\n- {編|あ}み{針|ばり}: knitting needle\n- {三|み}つ{編|あ}み: three-strand braid\n- {編|あ}み{目|め}: stitch (in knitting)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {編|あ}む: to knit, braid (interlocking loops/strands by hand)\n- {織|お}る: to weave (on a loom — different technique)\n- {縫|ぬ}う: to sew (with needle and thread)\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nKnitting ({編|あ}み{物|もの}) is a popular hobby in Japan. Hand-knitted scarves and sweaters are classic heartfelt gifts.",
